GFPGAN  (Apache License 2.0, with exceptions; optional face recovery)
https://github.com/TencentARC/GFPGAN        Copyright (C) 2021 THL A29 Limited, a Tencent company
================================================================================
Face recovery (--faces, and the "Restore faces" box in the window) runs the GFPGAN v1.4 network
(GFPGANv1.4.pth, 349 MB) that spandrel loads. The weights are NOT part of this repository or of the
.app/.dmg: they are downloaded from the GFPGAN releases only when the user asks for them, and checked
against a pinned SHA-256.

READ THIS BEFORE USING FACE RECOVERY COMMERCIALLY. GFPGAN's own LICENSE file says: "GFPGAN is licensed
under the Apache License Version 2.0 except for the third-party components listed below." Among those
components it lists:
  - StyleGAN2: "The codes are modified from the repository stylegan2-pytorch ... The official
    repository is https://github.com/NVlabs/stylegan2, and here is the NVIDIA license." That licence
    says the work "may be used or intended for use non-commercially", where "non-commercially" means
    "for research or evaluation purposes only".
  - DFDNet: "The codes are largely modified from the repository DFDNet. Their license is Creative
    Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International License."
The weights were also trained on face photographs (FFHQ), which carry their own terms. We have not
been able to establish whether these conditions reach the weights, or what they mean for a printing
business, and this project does not give legal advice. Face recovery is therefore off by default,
nothing is shipped, and the decision to use it, and for what, is the user's. The full GFPGAN LICENSE
is at the address above.

