================================================================================
Apple Vision and PyObjC
================================================================================
Faces and their landmarks are found with Apple's Vision framework, part of macOS, reached through
PyObjC (pyobjc-framework-Vision and its companions, MIT licence, listed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt
inside the .app). No face-detection model is shipped or downloaded.


================================================================================
Other dependencies (installed from PyPI, not vendored in this repository)
================================================================================
PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause style), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), Pillow (MIT-CMU), tifffile
(BSD-3-Clause), PyObjC (MIT) for face recovery, and optionally coremltools (BSD-3-Clause) for --engine ane. The
Tk GUI uses Python's tkinter (PSF license) and Tcl/Tk (Tcl/Tk license).

Binary builds bundle these packages. packaging/collect_licenses.py gathers the
license files they ship into THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt, which goes into the .app.

The interface text and its translations (English, Thai, Chinese, French) are
written for this project; they are drafts and welcome native-speaker review.
